### Describe the bug

In `--acp` mode, when a model call fails partway through an answer and the CLI retries it, the ACP client receives:
1. the failed attempt's partial answer;
2. `Info: Request failed due to a transient API error. Retrying...` as ordinary answer text;
3. the retry's full answer.

All three arrive as `agent_message_chunk` updates with no `messageId`. A client can't tell which text belongs to the abandoned attempt, so it shows, and saves, all three run together:

> This partial answer is cut off by the providerInfo: Request failed due to a transient API error. Retrying...This is the retried answer.

When every retry fails, the turn still ends with `stopReason: "end_turn"` and no error. The failure arrives only as answer text: `Error: Failed to get response from the AI model; retried 5 times (...)`.

**Frequency:** every time the model provider fails mid-stream. We hit it in normal use (HTTP 500 on the Responses WebSocket), and it reproduces every time against a local provider.

### Affected version

GitHub Copilot CLI 1.0.102-1, Windows x64.

### Steps to reproduce the behavior

1. Run an OpenAI-compatible provider. Its first `/chat/completions` stream sends a few content chunks, then `data: {"error":{"message":"Internal server error","type":"server_error","code":"internal_error"}}`; its second call succeeds. A script is below.
2. Start `copilot --acp --stdio` with `COPILOT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18741/v1`, `COPILOT_MODEL=fake-model` and `COPILOT_OFFLINE=true`.
3. Send `initialize` and `session/new`, then `session/prompt` with any text.
4. Watch the `session/update` notifications.

Observed with the script below: 9 `agent_message_chunk` updates of the partial answer, then one chunk `Info: Request failed due to a transient API error. Retrying...`, then 5 chunks of the retry's answer, then `end_turn`.

Variations of the same script (dropping the stream, returning HTTP 500, failing every call) give:

| Provider behaviour        | What the ACP client receives                                                                                                                                   |
| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Error event mid-stream    | partial chunks, then `Info: Request failed due to a transient API error. Retrying...`, then the retry's chunks                                                  |
| Stream dropped mid-stream | partial chunks, then `Info: Response was interrupted due to a server error. Retrying...`, then the retry's chunks                                               |
| HTTP 500 before streaming | the notice, then the retry's chunks                                                                                                                            |
| Every call fails          | five notices, then `Error: Failed to get response from the AI model; retried 5 times (total retry wait time: 15.63 seconds) Last error: 500 ...`, then `stopReason: "end_turn"` |

<details>
<summary>Fake provider (Bun)</summary>

```ts
// bun fake-provider.ts  → first completion fails mid-stream, later ones succeed
let calls = 0;
const sse = (o: unknown) => `data: ${JSON.stringify(o)}\n\n`;
const delta = (content: string, finish: string | null = null) =>
  sse({ id: `c${calls}`, object: "chat.completion.chunk", created: 0, model: "fake-model",
        choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { content }, finish_reason: finish }] });

Bun.serve({
  hostname: "127.0.0.1",
  port: 18741,
  async fetch(req) {
    const path = new URL(req.url).pathname;
    if (path.endsWith("/models"))
      return Response.json({ object: "list", data: [{ id: "fake-model", object: "model" }] });
    const fail = ++calls === 1;
    const words = (fail ? "This partial answer is cut off by the provider" : "This is the retried answer.").split(/(?<= )/);
    const body = new ReadableStream({
      async start(c) {
        const enc = (s: string) => c.enqueue(new TextEncoder().encode(s));
        for (const w of words) { enc(delta(w)); await Bun.sleep(40); }
        if (fail) enc(sse({ error: { message: "Internal server error", type: "server_error", code: "internal_error" } }));
        else { enc(delta("", "stop")); enc("data: [DONE]\n\n"); }
        c.close();
      },
    });
    return new Response(body, { headers: { "content-type": "text/event-stream" } });
  },
});
```

</details>

### Expected behavior

An ACP client can tell a retried model call apart from answer text and discard the abandoned attempt's output. Any of these would do:

- **A structured retry signal** instead of the `Info:` text, for example a `session/update` extension or `_meta` on the update. It would carry the attempt number and say that the previous attempt's output is void.
- **A `messageId` per model call** on `agent_message_chunk` and `agent_thought_chunk`, so a client can drop the superseded message. The SDK already gives each attempt its own `messageId` on `assistant.message_start` / `assistant.message_delta` and emits `assistant.turn_retry`, so the information exists inside the CLI.
- **When retries run out,** a `session/prompt` error, or at least a distinct stop reason, instead of `end_turn` with the failure written as answer text.

### Additional context

**The logs can't identify the failed request.** At the default level each failure gets one line:

```
[WARNING] [rust:model_events::producer] Model provider request failed {"stage":"inference","api_endpoint":"ws:/responses","http_status":500,"failure_kind":"http_error"}
```

It has no request or call ID, no provider error code or message, and no attempt number. With `--log-level debug` the failed attempt adds only `Upstream model error response shape (body content omitted) {...}`. A `Request-ID` is logged only for the successful response (`[rust:model_wire] response (Request-ID ...)`), while every full wire request, including the system prompt and the user's text, is written to the log. `events.jsonl` keeps only the successful attempt. Please add the provider's request ID (and `providerCallId` / `serviceRequestId`, which the SDK's event schema already defines) and the provider's error code to that WARNING line.

**Related:** #2101 and #2267 (the transient error itself), and #1627, #2914 and #3562 (retries exhausted). Those are about the failures; this issue is about how they're surfaced over ACP.

Suggested labels: `area:non-interactive`, `area:models`.

prs.body:
The language select in the stats footer always shows English, even on a localized page such as `/pl/data/`. The page text is translated correctly; only the select is wrong.

The select received the locale through `<select value={...}>`. Server rendering emits that as a `value` attribute, which browsers ignore for `<select>`, and no option was marked `selected`, so the first option (English) showed. During hydration, Solid does not apply the `value` property, so the select was never corrected on the client either.

The current locale is now marked with `selected` on its `<option>`. That renders into the server HTML, so the select shows the right language before any JavaScript runs.

### Verification

- Compiled the old and new markup with `babel-preset-solid` (hydratable SSR and DOM), rendered it on the server, and hydrated it in Chromium with Playwright. Before: `en` before and after hydration with locale `pl`. After: `pl` both times.
- `bun typecheck` in `packages/stats/app`, plus `oxlint` and `prettier --check` on the changed file.

### Visual

