Related: #172161

## What Problem This Solves

Keeps regression coverage for reusing `path find` results when TypeScript-style path mappings contain wildcard-looking keys and array values.

## User Impact

No additional runtime change: current main already handles literal-key quoting. The retained tests protect resolving and updating the returned array paths without changing neighboring mappings.

## Why This Change Was Made

Merged `d6d7435f59ec` to resolve the formatter and parser-test conflicts, preserving main's canonical implementation. The remaining diff is two test files: the in-process CLI-handler find -> array-node resolve -> `set --value-json` scenario for `*`, `**`, `@app/*`, and `types*`, plus four formatter round-trip cases not covered by the existing table.

## Evidence

- On 2026-10-17, built the native `cliStartup` / oc-path runtime successfully at `f596a8a321ba9e35220b0986705f4221f6ccd99a` and captured the actual shipped CLI flow below. All 11 independent CLI invocations exited 0. All four returned wildcard-looking array paths resolved and were updated with `--value-json`, preserving the other mappings after each write.
- The earlier 2026-10-16 native `test:extension oc-path --maxWorkers=1` run at this same head passed 33 files, with 348 tests passed and five existing tests skipped (Vitest 5.0.3, 30.41 seconds). The in-process handler scenario took 54 ms and the parser round-trip case 4 ms. Those are the previously recorded unit-test results, separate from this new CLI capture.
- Targeted formatting, whitespace, and the independent two-file source/commit review passed. The [hosted CI workflow at this head](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/38977462108) and its [`openclaw/ci-gate`](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/38977462108/job/117232489637) report success; selection-skipped jobs are not claimed as executed.
- The earlier local type-aware lint attempt stopped in SDK declaration preparation (insufficient resources, worker exit 13), and its subsequent local typecheck did not run. That local lane was not rerun for this capture. The earlier CLI autoreview attempt produced no report because its configured review engine was unavailable. The new build and CLI capture do not stand in for a full local test/release suite.

