Related: #159692

## What Problem This Solves

An admitted input whose transcript anchor is unavailable can retry the same unusable anchor and advance to another provider, even though a provider change cannot repair transcript continuity.

## User Impact

Stop that input after one failed attempt instead of repeating the same storage failure. Preserve its original error instead of trying to append a terminal assistant error through the invalid path. Genuine transient provider recovery remains unchanged. Input-specific failure-notice policy is intentionally a separate change; this PR does not claim to suppress every stale banner.

## Why This Change Was Made

Both missing-anchor emitters now produce a typed continuity failure. The existing native read-fence and writer-replacement errors, and exact serialized signatures, share one classifier. The SDK keeps these failures local; prompt/assistant handling and model fallback stop before unchanged-anchor response repair, account-health changes or another provider attempt. Existing cause/aggregate/suppressed error identities are retained.

The accepted-input owner's existing single admission refresh, original writer/session/entry/generation checks and side-effect replay barriers are unchanged. No recovery loop, replacement authority, schema, configuration or state store is added. #163655 already fixes the ordinary producer race; this is its remaining defensive failure-policy boundary, not another producer rewrite. #154904's dirty-index degradation policy and #182121's Workshop diagnostics are separate work and are not copied here.

## Evidence

Base: `2d2b4658943d94a0e7316924e67d73548c917538`. Signed candidate: `0a39437d9c30879c7cfa45eff2e89619fad31723`. Node24.22.1, isolated source Gateways, fixture-controlled loopback Responses transport; no live channel or real provider account used.

The regression **deliberately injects the exact serialized missing-anchor refusal at the canonical SDK message-persistence boundary after invoking the canonical captured-write assertion**. It does not claim the already-fixed ordinary producer race still reproduces. The existing native queued-input/late-promotion and original-input replay suites remain green.

| Captured Gateway outcome | Exact base owners | Signed candidate |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| SDK attempts for the refused input | 8 | 1 |
| Attempts under the configured fallback provider | 4 | 0 |
| Terminal assistant persistence attempts | 8 | 0 |
| Inference HTTP requests for that refused input | 0 | 0 |
| Returned HTTP status | 500 | 500 |

The healthy signed-candidate control made exactly one inference request and returned `CONTINUITY-HEALTHY-OK`. A transport proxy captured **14,443 request-body bytes and 1,291 received SSE-body bytes**; the response below is captured from the actual upstream HTTP reader, not copied from the fixture's scripted events. All three Gateway processes joined and all five Gateway/model/proxy listeners were independently closed. Twelve committed source/test file hashes, all seven base-owner overrides, signature and clean checkout verified after execution.

- Current-main RED: eight intended failures across SDK error identity, assistant response repair and provider-fallback boundaries.
- GREEN: **275 focused cases /12 files**:114 final-candidate consumer contracts and8 native queued-input/admission cases, plus153 producer/replay/side-effect/settled-tool/prefix cases retained across the serialized-native-name-only follow-up (their native/recovery paths were unchanged). Genuine provider failure recovery remains covered.
- Scoped sessions and owned-file types, type-aware core lint, format and whitespace passed. An optional broad agents leaf produced four off-scope benchmark/tooltip diagnostics; these are disclosed, not claimed baseline-attributed or green. Broad PR CI has not run yet.
- Optional local autoreview was unavailable due an existing authentication error; no validated review report is claimed and no credential repair was attempted.
- Independent source review and pr-simplify pass covered all changed lines and direct consumers; no actionable finding or justified simplification. Production +114/-6; tests +141/-0. The remaining growth is the shared classification and distinct SDK/retry/fallback boundaries, not a second recovery owner.
- Immediately before publication, current main `709b1a1ca3fe8179409004502b0491b853580d5e` retained identical blobs for all seven production owners; merge simulation was clean. The issue’s prior advisory still asks for an original queued-compaction reproduction: this PR does **not** supply that original ingress reproduction or claim to close #159692.
