## What Problem This Solves

ElevenLabs users can configure pronunciation dictionaries, but OpenClaw currently omits them from TTS requests, so those dictionary rules do not affect generated speech.

Fixes #182966

## Why This Change Was Made

The provider validates and forwards up to three ordered dictionary ID and version pairs for buffered and streaming synthesis. Empty or omitted lists preserve current requests, and input text is unchanged.

The provider-local configuration setting was approved for this PR on 2026-10-26.

## User Impact

Users can apply existing ElevenLabs pronunciation dictionaries through `tts.providers.elevenlabs.pronunciationDictionaryLocators`.

## Evidence

- Exact base/head loopback proof: `PROOF_MODE=base pnpm exec tsx production-runtime-proof.mts` and `pnpm exec tsx production-runtime-proof.mts` exercised the public `synthesizeSpeech` runtime through a registered ElevenLabs provider to the same local HTTP endpoint and with the same input.
- Base 608d44bfc49b438991ad6f1ef4c3e70eb0b51b96: the call returned 3 audio bytes but omitted locators; the four-entry input was accepted and made an HTTP request (2 to 3).
